    [
     1,
     "Hi Lyndal,<div><br></div><div>You can try:</div><div><br></div><div>library(dartR)<br>pcoa &lt;- gl.pcoa(<a href=\"http://platypus.gl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://platypus.gl&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792458133612000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0CsSJdDtvQG9x6g59EyPbi\">platypus.gl</a>)<br>gl.pcoa.plot(glPca = pcoa,<br>             x= <a href=\"http://platypus.gl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://platypus.gl&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792458133612000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0CsSJdDtvQG9x6g59EyPbi\">platypus.gl</a>,<br>             interactive = TRUE)<br><br>To open the documentation of the function, type in the R console a question mark followed by the function name, as shown below:</div><div><br>?gl.pcoa.plot<br></div><div><br></div><div>Make sure you have the latest version of dartR, by typing in the R console:</div><div><br></div><div>install.packages(&quot;dartR&quot;)<br></div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div>Luis </div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
